sidue","start":328,"end":328,"description":"Phosphoserine; in mitosis"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":401,"end":401,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":604,"end":732,"description":"Sufficient for interaction with GRB2"},{"type":"Region","start":619,"end":627,"description":"Required for interaction with CSK"},{"type":"Region","start":649,"end":770,"description":"Required for interaction with MYO6"},{"type":"Region","start":663,"end":671,"description":"Required for interaction with GRB2 and CSK"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":675,"end":675,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":709,"end":725,"description":"Sufficient for interaction with SH3KBP1 SH3 domain"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":723,"end":723,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":729,"end":729,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts (via NPXY motif) with DAB2 (via PID domain). Can interact (via PID domain) with LDLR, APP, APLP1 and APLP2, and weakly with INPP5D (via NPXY motifs); the interaction is impaired by tyrosine phosphorylation of the respective NPXY motifs. Can weakly interact (via PID domain) with LRP1 (via NPXY motif); the interaction is enhanced by tyrosine phosphorylation of the NPXY motif. Interacts with LRP2 (via NPXY motif); the interaction is not affected by tyrosine phosphorylation of the NPXY motif. Interacts with clathrin; in vitro can assemble clathrin triskelia into polyhedral coats. Interacts with AP2A2, ITGB1, ITGB3, ITGB5, PIAS2, DAB2IP, NOSTRIN, FCHO1, DVL3, EPS15, ITSN1 and EPS15L1. Interacts with SH3KBP1 (via SH3 domains). Interacts with GRB2; competes with SOS1 for binding to GRB2 and the interaction is enhanced by EGF and NT-3 stimulation. Interacts with MAP3K7; the interaction is induced by TGF-beta stimulation and may mediate TGF-beta stimulated JNK activation. Interacts with AXIN1 and PPP1CA; the interactions are mutually exclusive. Interacts with the globular tail of MYO6. Interacts (via DPF motifs) with FCHO2; the interaction is direct and required for DAB2-mediated LDLR endocytosis. Interacts with LRP6; the interaction involves LRP6 phosphorylation by CK2 and sequesters LRP6 towards clathrin-mediated endocytosis. Associates with the TGF-beta receptor complex (Probable). Interacts with SMAD2 and SMAD3; the interactions are enhanced upon TGF-beta stimulation. Interacts with GRB2; the interaction is enhanced by EGF and NT-3 stimulation. Interacts with SRC; the interaction is enhanced by EGF stimulation"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P98082-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":552,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000339788.10","ENST00000908971.1","ENST00000908974.1"],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,229],[230,448,323]],"edits":[{"start":230,"end":447,"original":"ESKDILLVDLNSEIDTNQNSLRENPFLTNGITSCSLPRPT","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":218,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":2,"foldedMissing":2,"features":[[5,218,0],[6,3,0],[7,3,0],[8,1,0],[9,1,0],[10,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P98082-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P98082-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":60.4,"plddt":[[50,1],[0,2],[50,4],[0,14],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,6],[50,1],[70,2],[90,106],[70,1],[90,34],[70,7],[50,7],[0,3],[50,1],[0,3],[50,3],[0,1],[50,1],[0,11],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,9],[50,2],[0,3],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,4],[50,1],[0,19],[50,1],[0,6],[50,1],[0,31],[50,1],[0,1],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,19],[50,1],[0,9],[50,1],[0,4],[50,3],[0,3],[50,1],[0,22],[50,1],[0,4],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,2],[50,3],[0,8],[50,3],[0,1],[50,3],[0,4],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,1],[50,17],[70,4],[50,1],[70,1],[50,11],[0,14],[50,8],[0,6],[50,1],[0,1],[50,14],[0,3],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,21],[50,1],[0,21],[50,6],[70,1],[50,1],[0,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"P98082-3","name":